spec workflow   │ Suggested Plan                                      │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ Wire OpenWrt ZeroClaw to host gRPC bridge           │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ Context (already true)                              │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ • Router mesh up: 100.69.0.3, host fabric via       │\n  │   egress: 10.0.0.2 pings OK.                        │\n  │ • Host op-grpc-bridge listens on 10.0.0.2:8090      │\n  │   (also 127.0.0.1 / 10.200.0.2).                    │\n  │ • Router scaffold exists: /etc/init.d/zeroclaw      │\n  │   (router) → /fast/zeroclaw/bin/zeroclaw gateway    │\n  │   start --port 42617, config/state dirs empty.      │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ • OpenWrt is musl armhf. Local artifact             │\n  │   /tmp/zeroclaw-armv7/zeroclaw is glibc             │\n  │   (ld-linux-armhf.so.3) — will not run              │\n  │   natively. Prior musl zigbuild failed on           │\n  │   duplicate crt1 _start.                            │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ mermaid flowchart                                   │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ flowchart LR                                        │\n  │   routerZC[router_ZeroClaw_gateway_42617]           │\n  │   nm[netmaker_100_69]                               │\n  │   egress[host_svc0_egress]                          │\n  │   bridge[op_grpc_bridge_10_0_0_2_8090]              │\n  │   routerZC -->|"HTTP/gRPC client"| nm --> egress    │\n  │ --> bridge                                          │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ Approach (locked)                                   │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ Native musl binary on /fast/zeroclaw, driven by     │\n  │ existing procd init — not Docker. Client target     │\n  │ is fabric IP http://10.0.0.2:8090 (mesh egress),    │\n  │ not public VPS IP and not 100.69.0.1.               │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ Steps                                               │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ 1. Produce a musl armv7 ZeroClaw binary from        │\n  │    /home/jeremy/zeroclaw                            │\n  │    (/home/jeremy/zeroclaw)                          │\n  │   • Fix zig linker wrapper so rustc CRT objects     │\n  │     are not double-linked (drop zig’s crt1 /        │\n  │     pass -nostdlib/-fno-entry style flags as        │\n  │     appropriate — same duplicate _start failure     │\n  │     seen in /tmp/zeroclaw-zigbuild.log).            │\n  │   • Build release                                   │\n  │     armv7-unknown-linux-musleabihf.                 │\n  │   • Smoke: file must show ld-musl-armhf or          │\n  │     statically linked musl.                         │\n  │ 2. Install onto router                              │\n  │   • Copy binary → /fast/zeroclaw/bin/zeroclaw.      │\n  │   • Init config under /fast/zeroclaw/config via     │\n  │     zeroclaw config init (or minimal                │\n  │     config.toml) with bridge/base URL               │\n  │     http://10.0.0.2:8090 for whatever               │\n  │     OpenAI-compatible / control-plane keys the      │\n  │     CLI expects (OPENCLAW_BASE_URL / provider       │\n  │     base_url pattern from the handoff).             │\n  │   • HOME / state stays /fast/zeroclaw/state per     │\n  │     init.d.                                         │\n  │ 3. Enable service                                   │\n  │   • /etc/init.d/zeroclaw enable && start            │\n  │   • Confirm listen on 42617 and process up.         │\n  │ 4. Verify path                                      │\n  │   • From router: TCP/HTTP to 10.0.0.2:8090          │\n  │     (bridge).                                       │\n  │   • From router: local gateway 127.0.0.1:42617      │\n  │     responds.                                       │\n  │   • Confirm netmaker routes still prefer            │\n  │     10.0.0.2/32 via netmaker (do not steal back     │\n  │     onto wg0).                                      │\n  │ 5. Do not in this pass: Salad provider secrets      │\n  │    hunt, odbus plugin schema regen, or              │\n  │    chatbot↔zeroclaw integration build — those       │\n  │    stay server-side / later.                        │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ Key files                                           │\n  │                                                     │\n  │ • Router: /etc/init.d/zeroclaw,                     │\n  │   /fast/zeroclaw/{bin,config,state}                 │\n  │ • Host bridge: already bound 10.0.0.2:8090          │\n  │ • Handoff facts: /home/jeremy/zeroclaw-server-w     │\n  │   iring-handoff.md (/home/jeremy/zeroclaw-serve     │\n  │   r-wiring-handoff.md)
