I'll try SSH to the router on the LAN and pull the firewall/zone and route info you asked for.\n\n  $ ssh -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -o BatchMode=yes root@192.168.1.1 'uci show\n    firewall | grep -E "zone|wg"; echo "---"; ip route' 1.5s\n    … 22 output lines hidden · ctrl+o to expand\n    192.168.0.0/24 dev wan proto kernel scope link src 192.168.0.169\n    192.168.1.0/24 dev br-lan proto kernel scope link src 192.168.1.1\n\n    Globbed "**/superpowers/**/SKILL.md" in .\n    Found 28 files\n\n  SSH to root@192.168.1.1 worked. Output:\n\n  uci show firewall | grep -E "zone|wg"\n\n  firewall.@zone[0]=zone\n  firewall.@zone[0].name='lan'\n  firewall.@zone[0].network='lan' 'wg0'\n  firewall.@zone[0].input='ACCEPT'\n  firewall.@zone[0].output='ACCEPT'\n  firewall.@zone[0].forward='ACCEPT'\n  firewall.@zone[1]=zone\n  firewall.@zone[1].name='wan'\n  firewall.@zone[1].network='wan' 'wan6'\n  firewall.@zone[1].input='REJECT'\n  firewall.@zone[1].output='ACCEPT'\n  firewall.@zone[1].forward='DROP'\n  firewall.@zone[1].masq='1'\n  firewall.@zone[1].mtu_fix='1'\n\n  ip route\n\n  default via 192.168.0.1 dev wan proto static src 192.168.0.169\n  10.0.0.0/24 dev wg0 scope link\n  10.0.0.0/24 dev netmaker metric 1\n  10.0.0.2 dev netmaker metric 1\n  10.189.0.0/24 dev wg0 scope link\n  100.69.0.0/24 dev netmaker proto kernel scope link src 100.69.0.3\n  172.17.0.0/16 dev docker0 proto kernel scope link src 172.17.0.1 linkdown\n  192.168.0.0/24 dev wan proto kernel scope link src 192.168.0.169\n  192.168.1.0/24 dev br-lan proto kernel scope link src 192.168.1.1\n\n  Takeaway: wg0 is already in the lan zone with input/forward = ACCEPT, so zone firewall isn’t the SSH\n  blocker. Traffic to 10.0.0.2 is steered to netmaker (10.0.0.2 dev netmaker metric 1), not wg0.
\\n  Results from the router:\n\n  1. Bridge reachability — OK\n\n  PING 10.0.0.2: 2/2 received, ~158 ms RTT\n  wget http://10.0.0.2:8090/ → Connecting… Download completed (0 bytes)\n\n  (curl isn’t installed; BusyBox wget succeeded.)\n\n  2. Dropbear listen — all interfaces\n\n  tcp  0.0.0.0:22  LISTEN  dropbear\n  tcp  :::22       LISTEN  dropbear\n\n  Not interface-bound. SSH bind isn’t why WG SSH fails.\n\n  3. Netmaker tunnel — healthy\n\n  peer … endpoint 129.153.134.63:51823\n    allowed ips: 100.69.0.2/32, 10.0.0.0/24\n    latest handshake: ~1m38s\n  peer … endpoint 188.68.58.237:51821\n    allowed ips: 100.69.0.1/32, 10.0.0.2/32\n    latest handshake: ~1m45s\n\n  Bottom line: Router ↔ bridge over netmaker works (ping + :8090). Dropbear listens on 0.0.0.0:22, so WG\n  SSH is likely blocked elsewhere (path/firewall on the peer side, or traffic arriving on wg0 vs\n  netmaker).
