Revise the existing Kiro spec at\n  `.kiro/specs/zeroclaw-router-wiring/` in place.\n  Do NOT implement on the router. Spec-only. Do NOT\n  invent a second identity control plane.\n  ## Problem\n  The current package is marked "Ready for\n  Implementation" but is unsafe / incomplete as a\n  locked-topology mission. Fix the documents so they\n  match Active topology and the identity handoff\n  residual-risk rules.\n  ## Related authority (read first, do not contradict)\n  - `.kiro/specs/README.md` — Active topology lock\n  - `.kiro/specs/3tched-ghostbridge-control-plane/` —\n  CF / mail / mesh / OpenFlow / enroll\n  - `.kiro/specs/netmaker-xray-identity-handoff/` —\n  Oracle decoy WG, signed assertion, HumanPrincipal,\n  bridge sole validator; ghostbridge self-asserted\n  headers are residual risk, not the product path for\n  new edge clients\n  ## Issues to fix (all of them)\n  1. **Stop shipping the weak identity path as the\n  product path**\n     - Remove durable hardcoded\n  `x-ghostbridge-footprint` and\n  `x-ghostbridge-trace-id` values from\n  requirements/design/tasks.\n     - Router→bridge auth must use the assertion /\n  HumanPrincipal model (or a clearly scoped temporary\n  lab mode labeled residual-risk, expire-by date, out\n  of Active). Prefer the real path.\n  2. **Close the LAN trust expansion**\n     - Do not leave `0.0.0.0:42617` + `require_pairing\n  = false` as default production.\n     - Default bind mesh/loopback-only or require\n  pairing / auth for LAN.\n     - Document who may call the gateway and with what\n  capability grants.\n  3. **Reconcile transport with topology lock**\n     - Active lock: mesh-private gRPC at\n  `10.0.0.2:8090`.\n     - Current draft assumes plain HTTP OpenAI `/v1`\n  with static headers.\n     - Either justify HTTP `/v1` as a bridge surface\n  that still goes through the same auth gate, or\n  re-spec to the real bridge surface. No hand-waving.\n  4. **No secrets in git**\n     - Footprints, trace-ids, keys, tokens:\n  placeholders + ops provisioning steps only.\n     - Never commit live host identity material.\n  5. **Complete the package**\n     - Add `boundaries.md` (non-negotiable / repudiated\n  / external assumptions / residual risks).\n     - Update status: not "Ready for Implementation"\n  until blockers cleared; use something like "Draft —\n  blocked on identity/auth redesign".\n     - Add this spec to `.kiro/specs/README.md` under\n  the correct section (Active vs Incomplete).\n     - Align requirements ↔ design ↔ tasks; tasks must\n  be independently verifiable and must not instruct\n  pasting secrets.\n  6. **Cross-links**\n     - Explicitly own: router ZeroClaw edge wiring\n  only.\n     - Defer to identity handoff for assertion\n  crypto/validation.\n     - Defer to control-plane for public CF / REALITY /\n  mail / OpenFlow IP:port.\n     - Do not reintroduce host `wg-lan`, CF tunnels\n  into CP, or SNI front on public `:443`.\n  ## Deliverables\n  Update in place:\n  -\n  `.kiro/specs/zeroclaw-router-wiring/requirements.md`\n  - `.kiro/specs/zeroclaw-router-wiring/design.md`\n  - `.kiro/specs/zeroclaw-router-wiring/tasks.md`\n  - `.kiro/specs/zeroclaw-router-wiring/boundaries.md`\n  (new)\n  - `.kiro/specs/README.md` (index entry)\n  ## Constraints\n  - Spec docs only; no router SSH, no live config\n  writes, no sudo, no service restarts.\n  - Fail-closed auth; no fallback to weaker headers\n  when assertion/auth fails.\n  - Keep verified mesh reachability facts that are\n  still true; mark unverified claims as unverified.\n  - End with a short "What changed / remaining\n  blockers" section in requirements.md.
